    // ── end front 35 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // ── front 36 — layout ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // `Layout` is the `§ 5` vocabulary: the eleven display values as the
    // section's OWN leaves (so `.Layout.Flex` keeps its pre-36 spelling), then
    // one sub-section per property group. `Inset` is the only numeric family
    // here and it is a MULTIPLIER of `--spacing`, exactly like front 35's
    // `Pad`/`Margin` — `.Layout.Inset.T.4` and `.Pad.T.4` read the same length
    // because both answer `spacing(4)`. `Gap` is front 37's; `Pad`, `Margin`,
    // `Size` and `Space` are front 35's, even where they space things the same
    // way.
    Layout {
